SC["a4c25_design"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER TWENTY-FIVE — THE COUNTER-PATTERN`)+P(`It takes nine days, and it is the best work of your life, and for most of it you forget to be afraid.`)+P(`Suyin clears a side-gallery of the warp and the two of you build the counter-pattern there in miniature, the way Tang builds a banquet in a teacup first: a model warp, forty lines, one handspan of held “sky.” She brings forty years of craft; you bring the gold and the outside eye; and between you, line by argued line, the new design stops being a thesis and starts being a THING, hanging in the lamplight, working.`)+P(`The architecture, when it finally stands clear, is almost insultingly simple. Willing tithe, Madam Xian's outward-running threads as the model: living weavers and resonants, each giving what Suyin gives but BRIEFLY, in rotation, a watch-rota for the sky instead of a life sentence. No dead pattern hoarded for centuries; the warp renews as the rota turns, so nothing goes brittle, so nothing needs the furnace-heat, so nothing needs the FUEL, so nobody sleeps in silk. The load per shoulder comes out — Ruan checks the figures three times, then a fourth time for the pleasure of it — lighter than a market-day's carry. The sky of the heartland, held up the way a village holds up a barn roof: everyone, a little, taking turns.`)+P(`It needs two impossible things, and you build toward both: a center that can hold itself, and a knot to tie it with.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The knot. The old books' name for it is the Sage's Shuttle.`,go:"a4c25_mountain"}]};

SC["a4c25_mountain"]={t:()=>P(`Every pattern you know is tied FROM OUTSIDE: your hands above the work, the weave below them. The Sage's Shuttle is the knot tied from inside — a pattern that includes its own weaver as a working line, self-tensioning, self-mending, alive where the old Loom is dead. Suyin can describe it. The black reel's oldest pages can diagram it. Nobody can tie it below the realm the books call Pattern Sage, and the books call the realm a legend, and the Lady, who reached it alone of everyone in four centuries, reached it on a night the sky was falling, and has never been able to say how.`)+P(`“Insight,” Suyin says. “All the realms are insight, but the last one is only insight. The thread's been in your hands since the riverbank, stitch. The realm is the moment you understand what you've been holding.”`)+P(`So you climb the mountain the only way anyone ever has: you sit with everything you know, and you let it argue.`)+((G.f.bg=="kata")?(P(`What rises, at the end of the ninth night, is the dojo. The kata you drilled ten thousand times until the day your body moved before thought — and the old instructor's one correction, the one you never understood at fourteen: <i>stop performing the form. The form is not in front of you. You are IN it.</i> You have been weaving the way you once fought: technique held at arm's length, executed ON the world. The Shuttle is the correction. The weaver inside the form. You feel the last understanding settle into place like a stance finally taken with the whole body.`)):(""))+((G.f.bg=="music")?(P(`What rises, at the end of the ninth night, is the melody. Eight bars, unresolved for two worlds and three acts — and you finally hear WHY it never resolved: you kept writing it from outside, a composer above the staff, hunting the missing note among the keys. The resolution was never a note. It's the moment the player stops playing the music and the music plays THROUGH — instrument, hand, and song one continuous string. The Shuttle is the resolution. The weaver inside the chord. The eight bars close, at last, somewhere under your sternum, and stay closed.`)):(""))+((G.f.bg=="code")?(P(`What rises, at the end of the ninth night, is the cube — and the day you stopped solving it. Algorithms all the way down, you used to say: state, operator, state, the solver outside the system, grinding. But the day it went QUIET in your hands you weren't running algorithms anymore; the cube and the solution and the solver had collapsed into one process with no outside. Fixed point. The function that takes itself as an argument and HOLDS. The Shuttle is exactly that knot: the weaver as a term in his own pattern. You feel the recursion ground itself, and stop, and stand.`)):(""))+((G.f.bg=="sister")?(P(`What rises, at the end of the ninth night, is the porch light. You always thought of it as hers — a thing she kept burning FOR you, from inside the house, while you were out in the dark. But you kept it too. Every night you came home was a night you'd chosen to be the kind of brother a light gets left on for; the light held you both, from inside both of you, neither one the keeper. That is the whole secret, and you have known it since you were nine. A bond is not tied from outside. The Shuttle is a porch light. The weaver inside the pattern, kept and keeping, both at once.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Open your eyes. The realm is RIGHT THERE, and there are two ways through the last door.`,req:()=>(G.insight>=14),rq:"(needs Insight 14)",go:"a4c25_clean"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Open your eyes. The understanding is close but not whole, and the sky won't wait for whole. Pay the difference yourself.`,hide:()=>(G.insight>=14),go:"a4c25_paid"}]};

SC["a4c25_clean"]={t:()=>P(`It doesn't feel like breaking through. It feels like a door you'd been pushing on swinging open at a touch, because it was never locked, because you are done mistaking the door for a wall.`)+P(`The world's threads do not change. YOU change, one notch, at the root of the seeing: every line in the side-gallery — the model warp, Suyin's fan, the lamp-smoke, the lake's pressure on the crystal, the slow tide of ten thousand reels — resolves into one continuous fabric with no outside edge, and you are a line in it, gold, taut, HELD, and holding. You always were. That's the realm: not power. Position.`)+SYS(`BREAKTHROUGH — clean, at the summit of understanding. (a4_counter: clean)`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Rise.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_counter="clean";realmUp();learn("counter","Counterweave");},go:"a4c25_sage"}]};

SC["a4c25_paid"]={t:()=>P(`Suyin's voice, very quiet: “There is a second way. The books don't recommend it. I do not recommend it. But it's mine to teach, because it's the one I used.” A breath. “You don't UNDERSTAND your way through the door. You weave part of yourself into it, and the door counts it as understanding, because in the oldest grammar they are the same word. It costs what it costs forever, stitch. Some things don't mend, even on us.”`)+P(`You think of six days, and a white boat, and a sky with a deadline, and you say what she said forty years ago, on a courtyard, eldest, with the Weave tearing overhead: somebody has to. You take three threads of your own substance — not qi; SELF, the warm load-bearing stuff the hammock-sleepers were farmed for — and you tie the last understanding out of your own line.`)+P(`It hurts in a way that doesn't end when it stops. The door opens. The world resolves into one fabric with no outside edge, and you are a line in it: slightly, permanently thinner.`)+SYS(`BREAKTHROUGH — paid for in self. Max HP −2, forever. (a4_counter: paid)`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Rise.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_counter="paid";G.maxhp-=2;G.hp=Math.min(G.hp,G.maxhp);realmUp();learn("counter","Counterweave");},go:"a4c25_sage"}]};

SC["a4c25_sage"]={t:()=>P(`PATTERN SAGE. The fifth realm; the one the books call legend; population, as of this lamplit morning under a lake: two.`)+P(`Suyin teaches you the realm's first verb before you've stopped shaking, because she is her sister's sister and believes in work. A frayed line in the model warp — she fraying it deliberately, with an apology to the model — and your hands moving on instinct that is no longer exactly instinct: not Mend, which patches from outside; not Unravel, which judges from outside; but the Sage's own stitch, run from INSIDE the fabric, where a tear is just a place the pattern has forgotten itself, and forgetting can be reminded. Gold runs down the frayed line and the line does not knit so much as REMEMBER, and the mend leaves no scar because, in the pattern's own grammar, nothing happened.`)+P(`“Counterweave,” Suyin names it, dry as her sister. “The Court's whole furnace, four hundred years and a thousand souls a generation, and the answer was one boy standing in the right place inside the cloth. I'd laugh, stitch, but I'm WOVEN to this thing; it shakes the province.”`)+((G.f.bg=="kata")?(P(`You move through the new realm's first hour the way you moved the morning after your first full kata: sore, lit, and unable to stop touching the world to feel it answer.`)):(""))+((G.f.bg=="music")?(P(`You spend the new realm's first hour listening: the city's tide of thread has KEYS now, modulations, and the Great Fray below is not a roar anymore but a specific, answerable dissonance, eight bars from home.`)):(""))+((G.f.bg=="code")?(P(`You spend the new realm's first hour reading the Loom like source: four hundred years of patches, the dead weight, the heat-budget — and, everywhere, the comments of a designer who knew it was bad and shipped anyway, because the sky was falling.`)):(""))+((G.f.bg=="sister")?(P(`You spend the new realm's first hour holding the new sense up to the one thread no realm has ever shown you — the one that runs OFF the world's edge, toward a porch light — and for the first time, at the very limit of the new seeing, it does not read as cut. It reads as HELD, from the far side.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Now the bill. The model works. The full pattern needs the one thing the model didn't: the center.`,go:"a4c25_bill"}]};

SC["a4c25_bill"]={t:()=>P(`That evening, over the model warp, Suyin lays out the cost the design has been hiding in plain sight, and her voice never once leaves silk.`)+P(`“The crossover. The old Loom can't simply be cut: the sky drops in the gap. The new pattern can't anchor into LIVE warp: the old tension would tear it apart half-tied. So for the length of the tying — an hour, maybe two — the heart-position of the Grand Loom must be held EMPTY of the old pattern and OPEN to the new. A gap, weaver. A held gap, in the middle of a quarter-million screaming lines, while you tie the Shuttle across it.”`)+P(`“Held by what?” you ask, already knowing.`)+P(`“By whom.” She does not look away; she has never once looked away from anything, you suspect, and that is what forty years in a machine does to courage. “Someone stands in the heart-position through the crossover. Old pattern dying around them, new one not yet alive. Whoever holds it will be holding by pure self, with no pattern to carry the load, and if the tying runs long the gap SPENDS them, as the old Loom spends fuel. You need the strongest holder alive, and the Court has spent four centuries making sure there is exactly one of those, and you are standing in her gallery, and she is half-woven into the thing that has to die.”`)+P(`The lamp burns. The model holds its handspan of sky, perfectly, on willing thread.`)+P(`“The Lady will convene the Reels the moment we touch the warp: the Loom is her body; she'll feel the first knot. So it happens in front of all of them or not at all.” Suyin begins, with terrible calm, to tidy the workbench. “Sleep, stitch. Tomorrow we go ask the Court's permission to save it. Bring your whole arithmetic. They'll bring theirs.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The Reels convene at dawn.`,go:"a4c26_convene"}]};